1
00:00:18,053 --> 00:00:20,015
I trust you had a fruitful day.

2
00:00:20,077 --> 00:00:23,402
I do not say happy, though I'm sure it has been a happy one.

3
00:00:24,484 --> 00:00:32,759
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambhudasa.

4
00:00:32,779 --> 00:00:40,332
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambhudasa.

5
00:00:41,189 --> 00:00:57,792
Hommage to the Buddha, the blessed, noble and fully self-awakened one.

6
00:00:59,716 --> 00:01:02,238
It's getting cold.

7
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:05,183
Almost like winter up here.

8
00:01:05,224 --> 00:01:08,087
What to do?

9
00:01:08,588 --> 00:01:09,609
Lots of rain too.

10
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:17,417
I thought we would have a little light relief this evening with the story of Angulimala.

11
00:01:18,018 --> 00:01:25,266
Now, I think most of you will know about Angulimala, but there's actually a whole discourse on him.

12
00:01:25,766 --> 00:01:29,049
He's the good thief in the Christian tradition.

13
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:35,817
He's the really bad fellow who converts his life and becomes fully liberated.

14
00:01:37,118 --> 00:01:40,643
So the back story, as they say these days,

15
00:01:41,382 --> 00:02:09,633
is that he was the son of a minister at the court of king pasenadi so remember he's the king up in in kosla which is north north india above the ganges way above and uh he is um studying at taxila so we mentioned this university town uh up in up in near ralpindi uh north pakistan today and um

16
00:02:11,234 --> 00:02:15,038
seemingly he was a great student and all the other students were very jealous of him.

17
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:26,977
So they spread rumours about him, even to the point of committing adultery or having sex with his wife, the professor.

18
00:02:27,737 --> 00:02:33,064
And for that, the professor asked him for an honorarium.

19
00:02:34,007 --> 00:02:38,473
So that's the word they use here.

20
00:02:39,127 --> 00:02:48,356
Although the teaching was given free, there was presumed payment at the end of all the teachings, something of that nature.

21
00:02:48,877 --> 00:03:00,250
So he asked him, of course, for a thousand fingers, little fingers from the right hand of human beings.

22
00:03:00,949 --> 00:03:07,616
So when Angulimala left, he felt obliged to

23
00:03:08,152 --> 00:03:11,076
well, to make good this honorarium.

24
00:03:11,097 --> 00:03:16,564
So he began terrorizing this territory in the kingdom of Pasenadi.

25
00:03:17,705 --> 00:03:19,087
And he was known as a murderer.

26
00:03:19,269 --> 00:03:21,050
Anyway, we'll take the story up then.

27
00:03:21,091 --> 00:03:28,221
So the Buddha is in fact in Sabati, that's the capital of Kosala.

28
00:03:30,849 --> 00:03:44,849
On that occasion, there was a bandit in the realm of King Pasenadi of Kosala named Angulimala, which means necklace of fingers, who was murderous, bloody handed, given to blows and violence, merciless to living beings.

29
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,414
Villages, towns and districts were laid waste by him.

30
00:03:48,816 --> 00:03:53,581
He was constantly murdering people and he wore their fingers as a garland.

31
00:03:55,425 --> 00:03:56,165
Now,

32
00:03:57,765 --> 00:04:01,331
The Blessed One had heard that his mother was going to go out.

33
00:04:01,993 --> 00:04:11,550
And again, the story is that he was just one finger short of the tally of 1000.

34
00:04:13,234 --> 00:04:19,925
So the Blessed One, presumably to safeguard his mother, went out to meet him.

35
00:04:20,766 --> 00:04:48,951
so he takes his roving bowl etc and out he goes now on the way the cow heard shepherds and plowmen passing by saw the blessed one walking along the road towards angulimala and said to him don't take that do not take that road recluse on this road is the bandit angulimala who is murderous bloody-handed given to blows violence and merciless to living being and uh they told him this about three or four times but of course uh the buddha walked on

36
00:04:50,668 --> 00:04:55,514
Now, when Angulimala saw the Blessed One coming from a distance, he thought, oh, it's wonderful.

37
00:04:55,535 --> 00:04:56,355
This is marvelous.

38
00:04:56,836 --> 00:05:02,564
Men have come along this road in groups of 10, 20, 30, even 40, but still they have fallen into my hands.

39
00:05:03,125 --> 00:05:07,029
Now this recluse comes alone, unaccompanied, as if by fate.

40
00:05:07,911 --> 00:05:09,853
Why shouldn't I take the recluse's life?

41
00:05:10,334 --> 00:05:13,117
That's his last, that would be his last finger.

42
00:05:13,177 --> 00:05:20,187
So he took up his sword and shield, buckled down his bow and quiver and followed close behind the Blessed One.

43
00:05:22,444 --> 00:05:34,377
Now then the Blessed One performed such a feat of supernormal powers that the bandit Angulimala, though walking as fast as he could, could not catch up with the Blessed One, who was walking at a normal pace.

44
00:05:34,879 --> 00:05:36,403
So here we have a bit of magic, you might say.

45
00:05:38,762 --> 00:05:42,209
And Angulimala thought, this is amazing, this is wonderful.

46
00:05:42,348 --> 00:05:45,112
Formally, I could catch up even a swift element and seize it.

47
00:05:45,173 --> 00:05:49,661
I could catch up even a swift horse, a swift chariot, a swift deer.

48
00:05:50,221 --> 00:05:56,531
And though I'm walking as fast as I can, I cannot catch up with this recluse who's walking at his normal pace.

49
00:05:56,552 --> 00:05:58,574
So what can we make of that?

50
00:05:58,675 --> 00:06:00,778
Well, we have to take it as it comes.

51
00:06:02,161 --> 00:06:04,904
But the point is that at some point,

52
00:06:05,425 --> 00:06:08,430
the Angulimala says, stop, recluse, stop.

53
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:18,725
Now, Angulimala is the son of a Brahmin who's at the court of Pasenadi.

54
00:06:19,807 --> 00:06:34,369
So there's a, in my mind, there's a possibility that Siddhartha Gautama, as he was before he became the Buddha, would have met him at some point.

55
00:06:34,855 --> 00:06:38,398
And there might have been some recognition.

56
00:06:39,178 --> 00:06:43,362
So as he's coming on the road, there is some recognition as to who this is.

57
00:06:44,324 --> 00:06:49,088
And maybe even Angulimala will have heard of the reputation that the Buddha has.

58
00:06:49,709 --> 00:06:52,250
And Angulimala is not evil in himself.

59
00:06:52,711 --> 00:06:54,853
He's trying to fulfill this honorarium.

60
00:06:56,675 --> 00:07:03,781
And he would have known that to kill a recluse, and especially someone who was possibly fully liberated, wasn't the best thing to do.

61
00:07:04,014 --> 00:07:09,101
Because like everybody else, or most people of that age, he would have believed in rebirth.

62
00:07:09,543 --> 00:07:14,509
And that's not a happy destination for someone who kills a fully liberated being.

63
00:07:15,732 --> 00:07:19,276
Anyway, he does shout, stop, recluse, stop.

64
00:07:19,677 --> 00:07:23,762
And the Buddha turns and says, well, I have stopped Angulimala.

65
00:07:24,303 --> 00:07:25,345
You stop too.

66
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:30,192
Now, then the bandit Angulimala thought, hmm,

67
00:07:30,576 --> 00:07:34,502
These recluses, son of the Sakyam, speak truth, assert truth.

68
00:07:35,201 --> 00:07:42,730
But though this recluse still walking, he says, I have stopped, Angulimala, you stop too, supposing I question the recluse.

69
00:07:43,391 --> 00:07:48,117
So this awakens in Angulimala a certain inquisitiveness.

70
00:07:51,521 --> 00:07:54,204
So then he breaks into verse, you see.

71
00:07:55,399 --> 00:07:57,963
While you are walking, recluse, you tell me you've stopped.

72
00:07:58,043 --> 00:08:00,826
But now when I have stopped, you say that I've not stopped.

73
00:08:01,307 --> 00:08:03,370
I ask you then, oh recluse, about the meaning.

74
00:08:03,610 --> 00:08:06,012
How is it that you have stopped and I have not?

75
00:08:06,853 --> 00:08:08,677
Angulimala, I've stopped forever.

76
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:11,680
I abstain from violence towards living beings.

77
00:08:11,759 --> 00:08:14,863
But you have no restraint towards things that live.

78
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:17,947
That is why I have stopped and you have not.

79
00:08:19,970 --> 00:08:25,595
At long last, this recluse, a venerated sage, has come to this great forest for my sake.

80
00:08:26,336 --> 00:08:33,643
Having heard your standards, teach me the Dharma and I will indeed renounce evil forever.

81
00:08:34,583 --> 00:08:39,828
So that's a rather quick conversion.

82
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:46,796
Anyway, he was taken by the Buddha's presence and his words.

83
00:08:46,975 --> 00:08:48,778
So anyway,

84
00:08:49,096 --> 00:08:51,619
By the end of this stanza, he actually wants to become a monk.

85
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:55,143
And the Buddha says, come Bhikkhu.

86
00:08:55,803 --> 00:08:57,806
And that is how he became a monk.

87
00:08:57,826 --> 00:09:11,442
Now, in those very early days, if somebody wanted to join the Buddha as a monastic, the ordination was simply him saying, come and try.

88
00:09:11,557 --> 00:09:12,357
That was it.

89
00:09:13,019 --> 00:09:19,548
Later on, when there were Arahats, he established this taking refuge in the Buddha, Dharma and Sangha.

90
00:09:20,951 --> 00:09:24,076
And that would have been, which is what lay people do.

91
00:09:24,275 --> 00:09:26,099
And in fact, we do it every morning.

92
00:09:26,139 --> 00:09:28,201
Everybody does that, even the monks.

93
00:09:29,182 --> 00:09:31,606
But it was an ordination at that time.

94
00:09:31,991 --> 00:09:46,870
Later on, because of the many naughty things that monks and nuns did and the new rules, then there was a much lengthier ordination whereby all the rules were taken on.

95
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:51,115
Certain people could not join who had joined.

96
00:09:51,475 --> 00:09:59,804
So, for instance, one of the consequences of Angulimala is that a rule was made that you couldn't ordain anybody

97
00:10:00,038 --> 00:10:09,717
who was a convicted thief or murderer or whatever, at least until he had completed his sentence.

98
00:10:12,563 --> 00:10:20,460
So then he wandered back in stage, he went to Sarvati and he lived at Sarvati with the Buddha.

99
00:10:21,672 --> 00:10:28,542
Now, on that occasion, great crowds of people had gathered at the gates of King Pasenadi's inner palace, very loud and noisy.

100
00:10:28,842 --> 00:10:34,149
So they'd heard about this and they went to the king and said, look, this bandit Angulibala is in your realm.

101
00:10:34,169 --> 00:10:37,575
He's a murderer, he's bloody handed, give him the blows and so on and so forth.

102
00:10:38,275 --> 00:10:39,999
Now, the king must put him down.

103
00:10:40,058 --> 00:10:49,552
Then in the middle of the day, King Pasenadi of Kosala drove out of Savati with a cavalry of 500 men and set out for the park.

104
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:55,826
He drove as far as the road was passable for carriages and then he dismounted and went to the Blessed One.

105
00:10:56,707 --> 00:10:59,652
The Blessed One, of course, the Buddha would have heard all these horses.

106
00:11:00,231 --> 00:11:01,553
So he said, what is it, great king?

107
00:11:01,673 --> 00:11:04,697
Is King Seniya Bimbisara of Magadha attacking you?

108
00:11:05,178 --> 00:11:08,442
Or the Lichaves of Visali or other hostile kings?

109
00:11:09,583 --> 00:11:14,610
Oh, venerable sir, says, what's his name?

110
00:11:15,030 --> 00:11:15,912
Pasenadi.

111
00:11:16,229 --> 00:11:23,177
No, I'm not being attacked, but there's a bandit in my realm called Angulimala who is murderous, etc.

112
00:11:23,839 --> 00:11:26,602
And I shall never be able to put him down, Venerable Sir.

113
00:11:27,464 --> 00:11:43,485
Great King, says the Buddha, supposing you were to see that Angulimala had shaved off his hair and beard, put on the ochre robe and gone forth from home life into homelessness, that he was abstaining from killing living beings.

114
00:11:43,852 --> 00:11:55,105
taking what is not freely given, false speech with frailing from eating in the evening, and only one part of a day was celibate, virtuous and of good character.

115
00:11:55,705 --> 00:11:58,187
If you were to see him thus, how would you treat him?

116
00:11:58,808 --> 00:12:04,615
Oh, venerable sir, we would pay homage to him or rise up for him and invite him to be seated.

117
00:12:04,855 --> 00:12:09,600
We would invite him to accept robes, alms food and resting place on medicinal requisites.

118
00:12:10,301 --> 00:12:11,581
Or we would arrange for him

119
00:12:11,815 --> 00:12:14,499
lawful guarding, defense and protection.

120
00:12:15,801 --> 00:12:19,004
But Venerable Sir, he is an immoral man, one of evil character.

121
00:12:19,125 --> 00:12:22,269
How could he ever have such virtue and restraint?

122
00:12:24,552 --> 00:12:31,462
On that occasion, the Venerable, so he's already a monk, you see, the Venerable Angulimala was sitting not far from the Blessed One.

123
00:12:32,024 --> 00:12:38,633
And then the Blessed One extended his right arm and said to the king, great king, this is Angulimala.

124
00:12:40,402 --> 00:12:42,804
Now the king was frightened, alarmed and terrified.

125
00:12:42,865 --> 00:12:46,308
And knowing this, the blessed one said to him, don't be afraid, great king.

126
00:12:46,328 --> 00:12:47,070
Do not be afraid.

127
00:12:47,110 --> 00:12:49,113
There's nothing for you to fear from him.

128
00:12:50,354 --> 00:12:53,057
Then the king's fear, alarm and terror subsided.

129
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:59,524
And then the king says to him, venerable sir, is the noble lord really Angulimala?

130
00:12:59,846 --> 00:13:00,605
Yes, great king.

131
00:13:01,427 --> 00:13:04,071
Venerable sir, of what family is the noble lord?

132
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:05,852
Of what family is his mother?

133
00:13:06,433 --> 00:13:08,735
My father is Gaga, great king.

134
00:13:08,775 --> 00:13:10,138
My mother is Mantani.

135
00:13:10,826 --> 00:13:14,552
Then let the noble Lord Gagamantani put her rest content.

136
00:13:14,732 --> 00:13:18,679
I shall provide robes, arms food, resting place, medicinal requisites.

137
00:13:20,121 --> 00:13:27,553
Now, at that time, Angulimala was a forest dweller, an arms eater, an arms food eater, a refuse rag wearer.

138
00:13:27,594 --> 00:13:36,548
Remember, they took the shrouds from the corpses on the charnel grounds and sewed them into robes.

139
00:13:37,220 --> 00:14:00,543
restricted himself to three robes he replied enough great king my triple road is complete uh so what this shows you that uh even at that time anybody who was um dressed as a brahmin or as a cleric or one of these refuse um uh one of these uh people who've gone to homelessness

140
00:14:00,777 --> 00:14:05,244
a samana, a recluse, there was great respect for them.

141
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:22,931
I mean, I'm sure there was a bit more discussion before the king offered to make him robes and whatnot, but you can see that there was just a general respect for people who left the home life for homelessness.

142
00:14:25,254 --> 00:14:26,937
Anyway, the king now leaves.

143
00:14:27,371 --> 00:14:32,899
he's got, he is busy, we are busy and have much to do, he's using the royal plural there, we are busy.

144
00:14:33,879 --> 00:14:36,202
Now is the time great king, do as you think fit.

145
00:14:37,024 --> 00:14:40,128
Then King Pasenadi rose from his seat and went off.

146
00:14:40,488 --> 00:14:46,615
Now then it was morning and Venerable Angulimala dressed, taking his robe and outer robe, went to Sarvati for alms.

147
00:14:47,397 --> 00:14:52,283
As he was wandering for alms from house to house, he saw a certain woman, or he heard a certain woman,

148
00:14:53,022 --> 00:14:55,284
Giving birth to a deformed child.

149
00:14:55,304 --> 00:14:56,206
That's what it says here.

150
00:14:56,246 --> 00:15:06,442
But the commentary says having difficulty giving birth and was shouting and moaning and so on and so forth.

151
00:15:07,062 --> 00:15:10,167
And he thought to himself, how beings are afflicted.

152
00:15:10,267 --> 00:15:12,510
Indeed, how beings are afflicted.

153
00:15:13,773 --> 00:15:17,138
And then he came back to the Blessed One and he sat down to one side.

154
00:15:17,238 --> 00:15:22,184
Venerable Sir, he said to the Blessed One, I dressed and taking my robe and bowl, etc.,

155
00:15:22,503 --> 00:15:26,005
And I saw a certain woman giving birth, having trouble giving birth.

156
00:15:26,866 --> 00:15:30,990
When I saw this, I thought how beings are afflicted, how beings are afflicted.

157
00:15:31,571 --> 00:15:47,524
In that case, Angulimala, says the Buddha, go to Sarvati and say to that woman, sister, since I was born, I do not recall I've ever intentionally deprived the living being of life by this truth and asseveration.

158
00:15:48,265 --> 00:15:51,008
May you be well and may your infant be well.

159
00:15:52,287 --> 00:15:56,211
Venerable sir, said Angulimala, wouldn't it be telling a deliberate lie?

160
00:15:56,331 --> 00:16:00,197
For I have intentionally deprived many beings of life.

161
00:16:00,216 --> 00:16:17,659
Then Angulimala go to Savaki and say to that woman, sister, since I was born with the noble birth, in other words, since he ordained, I do not recall that I have ever intentionally deprived a living being of life by this asseveration, this truth.

162
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:20,403
May you be well and may your infant be well.

163
00:16:21,092 --> 00:16:50,052
yes venerable sir says and later on he went in and stood stood at the gate there or stood before the house so that at least she could hear what he said sister since i was born into the noble birth i do not recall that i have ever intentionally deprived the living being of life by this truth may you be well may your infant be well and then the woman and the infant were well so

164
00:16:50,388 --> 00:17:05,381
So even to this day, if you turn up at a monastery and tell the monks that you're pregnant, they can offer you this blessing if you wish it.

165
00:17:05,961 --> 00:17:07,723
Of course, it only applies to women.

166
00:17:09,085 --> 00:17:13,429
So it's still used today as a blessing.

167
00:17:17,873 --> 00:17:18,353
Anyway,

168
00:17:18,957 --> 00:17:37,045
And dwelling alone, withdrawn, diligent, ardent and resolute, the venerable Angulimala, realizing for himself with direct experience here and now entered upon and abided in that supreme goal of the holy life for the sake of which clansmen rightly leave from home into homelessness.

169
00:17:37,285 --> 00:17:39,608
Earth is destroyed, et cetera, et cetera.

170
00:17:39,628 --> 00:17:41,471
In other words, he becomes an Arahant.

171
00:17:42,613 --> 00:17:47,039
Now, then when it was morning, and this was after he became fully liberated,

172
00:17:47,611 --> 00:17:50,594
Taking his robe and bowl, he went into Sarvati for alms.

173
00:17:50,773 --> 00:17:56,179
Now on that occasion, someone threw a clod and hit the Venerable Angulimala's body.

174
00:17:56,578 --> 00:18:06,268
Someone threw a stick, someone threw a potsherd with blood running down from the cut in his head and his bowl broken and his outer robe torn.

175
00:18:06,288 --> 00:18:07,949
So in other words, the crowd attacked him.

176
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:16,217
He went to see the Blessed One and the Blessed One said to him, bear it Brahmin, bear it Brahmin.

177
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:28,314
you are experiencing here and now the result of deeds because of which you might have been tortured in hell for many years, for many hundreds of years, for many thousands of years.

178
00:18:28,334 --> 00:18:30,980
So this was obviously a consequence of his murders.

179
00:18:31,361 --> 00:18:34,307
There must have been lots of people who were still very, very angry.

180
00:18:37,932 --> 00:18:39,413
And then he went off.

181
00:18:40,615 --> 00:18:42,597
He was alone, retreat, experiencing bliss.

182
00:18:42,919 --> 00:18:48,006
So then he obviously left and lived out the rest of his life.

183
00:18:48,445 --> 00:18:52,132
And there's a whole verse here which tells the story, retells the story.

184
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:56,798
And there is one verse which we can take to heart perhaps.

185
00:18:57,759 --> 00:19:04,188
They are fools and have no sense who give themselves to negligence.

186
00:19:04,208 --> 00:19:07,752
And those of wisdom, but those of wisdom guard

187
00:19:07,919 --> 00:19:36,171
diligence and treat it as their greatest good so um this is a story where you know it gives us a bit of hope doesn't it uh somebody who uh commits terrible crimes although we have to remember he hasn't got the heart of evil he's he's he's repaying a debt even though it's a horrible way to to pay a debt uh he's able to you know in in the western sense repent uh

188
00:19:36,336 --> 00:19:46,907
and to convert, to change his way completely, and be overcome by remorse, and through the practice of vipassana, etc., find complete liberation.

189
00:19:47,488 --> 00:19:52,712
So if he can do it, I'm sure we can.

190
00:19:52,732 --> 00:20:01,761
So that's, just to repeat that verse for us, they are fools and have no sense, who give themselves to negligence, and those are good.

191
00:20:02,682 --> 00:20:05,465
So I hope that you found that little story

192
00:20:05,799 --> 00:20:22,492
inspiring and that you take up the cudgels of uh of our practice and that you will be liberated like angulimala in no length of time sooner rather than later so we can do a bit of practice

